; Generated by c64-source. Edit the values here: generate keeps them.
; The switches of the build. Each switch is 0 or 1: change a value, then build again.
; The defaults give the clean program: copy protection, trainers, cheats and
; changes of a crack are 0, and the fixes of the releases are 1.
; generate adds a new switch with its default and removes a switch that the
; knowledge does not have. The build of a release does not read this file.

; Copy protection: off by default
PROTECTION        = 0 ; on in DC, SAEGER, TBC. $0440-$0442, $06f1-$06f4, $166c-$1671, $1703-$170a, $1fce-$1fd2, $1fe5-$1fe9, $31a1-$31a3, $342a-$3430, $36a8-$36ad, $3ca9-$3cae, $5134-$5135, $5139-$513a, $517b-$517d. The copy protection checks of the original loader marks and the key page $CF00. Each patch takes the passing path with the same registers and flags.

; Changes of a crack: off by default
CRACK_DIABOLO     = 0 ; on in SAEGER. $4771-$4777. msg_presents reads DIABOLO  PRESENTS in SAEGER, DATASOFT PRESENTS in TBC and DC.

; Fixes of the releases: on by default
FIX_RAM_TEST_BYTE = 1 ; on in DC, TBC. $9b00-$9b00. $9B00 in the source of room charset C is $0F in TBC and DC and $55 in SAEGER. $55 is the first value that the KERNAL RAM test at $FD6E-$FD83 writes to each byte before it writes the old byte back: a reset in the test left it in the saved image. build_double_height_font copies the byte into the double-height charset at the cold start.

; Other changes
RUN_STATE         = 0 ; on in SAEGER. $e100-$e130, $e2e7-$e2e8, $e30a-$e314, $e3de-$e3e8, $e5e6-$e5e7, $e86c-$e86c. Values that a run of the game left in the music player before the SAEGER image was saved: the voice state at $E100, flags, the stream fetch operands and a branch operand. The game writes each before it reads it. TBC and DC have the values before any run.
TITLE_PICTURE     = 1 ; on in TBC. no patch. src/boot.asm shows the Datasoft title picture (src/title_picture.kla) before the loader starts the game. TBC shows the picture in its intro, with CRACKED BY TBC in the bitmap and one screen colour for all cells. SAEGER and DC do not hold it. The switch has no patch: the game bytes do not change.
